25,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Our budget is nearly a quarter lower than expected, and floor space fitting is now coming out of this fund.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Past trials show that call-backs significantly reduced readmissions for the elderly, but joint clinics often collapse due to budget disputes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Midori,,"We have a serious shortage of ward nurses, but the midwifery rota actually has some unusual slack.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The car park and rooms are full by mid-morning, and the booking system ignores any work without a fixed slot.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"External data agreements are taking over a year to sign, and shared nursing rounds often fail due to access issues.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, if data agreements take fourteen months, any program relying on outside surgeries will be delayed.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, and if the budget is tight, we cannot afford a program that doesn't generate its own tariff.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, if the booking system is that limited, we need a program with very clear, fixed appointments.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly, Midori! We can't have people just wandering in if the parking is already full.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, the slack in midwifery is interesting. Perhaps we can utilize that instead of stressing the ward nurses.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I also found that off-site contacts draw no tariff. We must prioritize on-site services to keep the budget viable.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, the failure of joint clinics suggests we should avoid programs split between two departments.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, that makes sense. If we use the midwifery slack on-site, it solves the staffing and tariff issues.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Kenji,,But we still have the room problem. Any on-site program needs a dedicated space that doesn't clash with others.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I agree. A single-department lead is much safer for long-term stability.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
