50,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The candidates are A: Home Follow-Up, B: Day Rehab, C: Perinatal Support, and D: Chronic Care. I lean toward B.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Shion,,"A and D rely on outside coordination or home visits, which I suspect are less effective or harder to track.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Midori,,"C uses the midwifery slack I found, which is a huge advantage for staffing.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Kenji,,B and C both need rooms. But B's rehab space might be too demanding for our current parking.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Shizue,,A and D face the data agreement and access hurdles I discovered. C is much more contained.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, does C provide a steady on-site tariff? If it's in-hospital, it fits my budget concerns.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, is C a joint program? If it's midwifery and pediatrics, it might suffer the ""joint clinic"" collapse.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Midori,,"It is joint, Shion, but the midwifery slack might provide the stability the previous joint clinics lacked.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, B would require a ""dedicated space,"" which might be too expensive given the ledger cuts.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, the perinatal focus is usually more cohesive than general joint clinics.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If B is too expensive to build and A/D are unfunded by tariffs, C is the most fiscally sound.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Shion,,"I still worry about the joint nature of C, but A and D are logically disqualified by the data delays.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Midori,,C is the only one that doesn't add pressure to our exhausted ward nursing staff.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"If C uses existing slots and the midwifery team, it's the easiest for the booking system to handle.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. It avoids the external surgery bottlenecks and the home-visit failures.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Shion,,I will vote for C as the least risky of the remaining options.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Midori,,I vote for C!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Kenji,,C it is!,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
